The Karate Kid, Master the Martial Arts.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:26.680
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.060
I'm Mike.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.660
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:32.520
Guys, today we are talking about The Karate Kid.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:38.180
Whether that's the movie, the second movie, the first video game, the only video game, you decide.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.660
I think it's the only video game.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.660
It's the only video game is correct.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.140
That there ever will be.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.640
That there ever will be probably for The Karate Kid unless somebody, you know, gets nostalgic for the Jaden Smith movie

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.900
and winds up making like an HD remaster but in video game form.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.120
Of the movie.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.100
There's no HD remasters of movies, right?

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.400
Unless they go back and scan the film and 4K.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.140
I mean, that's what they did with like DVDs and then they did that with Blu-rays.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.820
Do you think a DVD? But they never say like, we're remaking this movie from the ground up.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.480
Well, no, that's actually what...

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.620
That's just remaking a movie.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.540
Wasn't that Dracula? Dracula? No, not Dracula.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.940
What's that? Psycho.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.940
Oh, with Vince Vaughn. Remember the 1998 version?

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.400
With Vince Vaughn. It was a shot for shot remake.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:18.500
Oh, okay. Yeah.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.620
Just then corrected. It's like, why have a director?

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:21.940
Why did they hire that guy?

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:23.660
To make sure they did it right.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:27.560
Yeah. He must have been excited when he saw any kind of money in that paycheck.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.580
You know, like, wow, I just get away with this.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.000
It was actually Christopher Nolan, Mike.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:32.780
It was Christopher Nolan?

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.320
Yeah, he directed that. Before the following?

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.200
Yeah. Yeah, the following is Christopher Nolan's first film.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.640
For those of you that don't know, it's pretty good.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.920
Is it The Following or is it just The Following?

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.380
It's following, not The Following.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.460
The following is something I say when I get movies incorrect.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:47.880
Right, okay, good. Just checking.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:52.080
But since we're on the subject of movies, do we want to talk about the Karate Kid movie?

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.720
I would love to talk about the Karate Kid movie.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.140
Okay, so let's just focus on part one for right now.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.040
Yeah. And it's important why we even mention the other parts later on.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.780
But just part one, Sean, just take me through your feelings about the Karate Kid movie.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:11.860
All right, so Karate Kid was one of my cultural blind spots, like, up until a few days ago.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.440
I had never seen it.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.100
I only knew that, you know, Mr.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.740
Miyagi's a funny old man that says wax on, wax off, and

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.900
then there's a really goofy 80s fight at the end.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.360
And I didn't really give it much thought, didn't really want to see it.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:26.560
Then I had to see it.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.520
And I actually really liked the movie.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:35.740
It's a really fun movie, and it's not as goofy as I thought it would be because there's actual, like, heartwarming parts.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.460
Yeah, I actually, I don't remember a ton of it.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.360
It's just been a long time.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.140
But I do remember really liking it when I was a kid, and I imagine it holds up.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:50.960
Yeah. But I've actually seen, well, we weren't talking about this, but I've seen the next Karate Kid more than the one with, and I forgot her name.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:51.960
Who plays the? I don't know.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.240
You said it earlier. But that's not the next Karate Kid.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.500
That's the movie called The Next Karate Kid.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:58.380
That's what I mean. Yeah, yeah, yeah. Hilary Swank.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:02:59.680
Yeah, Hilary Swank.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.980
More than I've seen the original, but I have seen the original.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:05.220
Yes, yeah. And that's actually Karate Kid 4, the next Karate Kid.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.380
Right, yeah, yeah. I don't know why I saw that one, like, before I saw the original.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.600
That's fine. Yeah, I think it's interesting.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.700
Well, maybe you just had, like, a DVD copy of it.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.740
Yeah. I saw it on TV, like, multiple times or something.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.740
Laser disc? Maybe.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.920
Also, The Next Karate Kid came out in 94.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.240
Which is more of our time.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.620
Yeah, exactly. The other ones came out, like, mid-80s to late-80s.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.740
Anyway, I wanted to say, when it comes to the Karate Kid movie, upon re-watching it now,

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.420
you know, it kind of feels like Rocky Jr., right?

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.320
Yeah. Like, in many ways, especially his, Ralph Macchio's performance.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:38.360
It's really great.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:42.140
At times, yeah, it's really good, but it also reminds you of Sylvester Stallone a lot.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:45.840
Oh, yeah, he's got that, like, oh, I'm from New York, I'm from Jersey.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.280
Right, and that's not the problem with Sylvester Stallone, either.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:49.820
I'm not knocking his performance in Rocky.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.040
I think it's a great performance, too.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:54.220
So, I just think it's, like, funny that, like, it's almost like the kids needed a version

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:58.980
of Rocky to look up to, rather than watching, like, prize box fighting.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:02.800
So, they were like, let's just do a karate version for kids.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.880
Also, martial arts, pretty hot around this time, right?

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:10.420
Yeah. Like, I feel like everybody wanted to wear, like, a karate black belt.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:14.580
But was that because of, or because of Karate Kid?

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.060
I think it's because of Karate Kid.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:17.700
Okay. Yeah, if we're being honest.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.860
Also, one other tidbit, the Mr.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:26.800
Miyagi thing. So, I had a really good friend in high school, Mike Diagardi, and that's very Italian, that last name.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:31.280
And his dad, who was very Italian, looked just like Mr.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.260
Miyagi. And I didn't see the movie until I was in high school.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.840
And I just remember everybody calling him Mr.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.940
Miyagi and then watching the movie and just, like, blown away by not only, like, Mr.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:42.840
Miyagi's character,

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:48.660
but also, like, just that this man who's in the living room with us as we're watching the movie looks exactly...

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:49.840
You watched it with him?

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:52.680
Oh, Papa Dio is what we call that guy.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.180
Papa Dio. Yeah, he's a great guy.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.220
I thought you called him Mr. Miyagi.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:56.980
A lot of nicknames.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:01.140
A lot of nicknames for, yeah, one parent in the school system.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.640
So, that's Karate Kid Part 1.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.380
I don't think we're going to, like, do any more talking about that.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:11.820
I just want to say that, since I think we're seconding into talking about Part 2...

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:18.780
Yes. I didn't watch it because I just didn't have the time to, but I did read the Wikipedia article.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:25.140
And when I found out that they just threw Allie to the wayside just to get, like, a new leading lady...

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.940
Hey, she stood him up a prom.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.840
This is ridiculous. She wouldn't do that.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:29.940
She's Allie. Yeah.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.200
Also, like, it wasn't just stand him up.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.240
It was like, I left with another man.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.740
From UCLA. Like, no, Allie wouldn't do that.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:40.140
It also kind of, like, invalidates the whole, like, first movie.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:46.880
I watched the trailer for Karate Kid Part 2, and it was a lot of just, like, the whole promotional language was just,

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.880
this is the real karate movie.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.620
Like, the other one was fun and games.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:06:00.140
Now, and I mean, like, to be honest, yes, because at the end of Part 2, there's literally a fight to the death between Danny and Chozen.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.400
Chozen. Chozen, whatever.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.320
I don't... I think it's Chozen.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.720
Chozen one. Yeah, yeah.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.340
I just thought, like, if you were going to make that into a real name, it would be, like, Chozen.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:09.900
Sure. Yeah.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.600
I think Cho's more of a last name.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:12.960
But... Okay. Very cool.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.400
Joe, did you watch Part 2?

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.320
I did not. Okay.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.080
Never seen it, and I didn't watch it this time.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.420
I am very interested in this fight to the death, though.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.360
Yeah. Because it gives it, provides some context for the game we played.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.200
Well, you played it. Right. And that's a good point to get to, too.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:29.720
Yeah, because I have some things I'll mention later when we play it that I was surprised about.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.060
But now it's sounding from the movie.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:33.260
Maybe some of this stuff is not as out of place.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.960
Yeah, yeah. No, the movie definitely...

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:35.780
The movie definitely...

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:42.080
So, for those of you that are uninformed, the Karate Kid NES game is based on the Karate Kid Part 2.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:43.520
For the most part.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:48.260
Yeah, okay. I know what you're going to get to, but let's just save that for when we talk about the actual game.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.440
I know, but it's for the most part.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:50.700
It's barely true.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:52.900
It's for the most part. Yeah, but whatever. I don't know what you're talking about.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:53.860
Yeah, yeah. Don't worry about it. I can't wait.

00:06:53.860 --> 00:07:01.240
So, if you didn't see the Part 2 movie, like most people probably, because the box office differential is quite large between Part 1 and Part 2.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:06.960
Oh. If you didn't see Part 2, there's a good chance that you bought the Karate Kid Part 1 and were thinking, like, what's...

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.200
Like, this isn't what I remember.

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:11.320
But also, like, I guess you wouldn't care, right?

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.640
You're just playing as Danny kicking up a bunch of...

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:16.000
Yeah, I feel like at this time...

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.620
Guys. Guys, yeah.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:25.620
I feel like at this time, buying a video game based on a movie, you're generally not expecting it to follow the movie necessarily, even at all.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.560
Yeah. I'd say so.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:36.800
Yeah, well, even in the game's manual, it lets you know, like, right off the bat, that, like, there's only three enemies in this game.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:44.640
There's Chosen, Chosen's, like, henchmen, and then guy with, like, a guy with a spear.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.400
Yeah, guy with a spear is pretty crazy.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.560
The spear was the thing that I was...

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:52.940
Is that in the movie? I was like, I thought we were in, like, a karate tournament and I was, like, training, and then these guys come out with spears at me.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.540
Right, well, we'll have to get there.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.940
Yeah. Yeah, because I'd like to do it chronologically, but yeah.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:59.060
Sure, sure. So, let me put it this way.

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:08.140
I don't remember Ralph fighting anybody with spears in the movie, but it wouldn't surprise me if they were in the area or environment.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.120
Yeah. They're in the background guys with spears.

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.240
Yeah, exactly. And then they just figured, oh, those guys have been good enemies.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:16.240
But now somebody at home can remind us of, like, that entire cutscene.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:21.140
Yeah. Cutscene. The entire part of the movie where he fought five guys with spears.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:22.960
So, just go ahead and call us out.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:24.680
Five guys. Okay.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.320
First impressions on the game.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.340
Sean? It's pretty jank.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:36.140
My first impression was this is jankier than Jaws, and it's also jankier than Goonies.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:43.300
But I also liked that it was sort of just throwing you between scenes from the movies.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:48.260
I knew that there were scenes from the movies even after the first level.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:56.380
But I thought that was a different way to do it instead of just throwing them into a completely different situation that never happened in the movies a la Goonies.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:58.840
But yeah, that's my first impression.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:07.560
Joe? So, first off, I thought these controls are very sticky and, like, hard to do.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:10.480
Yeah. That was the first thing that jumped out at me, and it never went away.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:12.160
I just got used to it eventually.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:16.220
But the controls being aggravating was the first thing that jumped out at me.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:17.740
And I don't mean, like, the actual...

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:20.200
I mean, some of it is, like, the actual what inputs you need.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:23.840
But it's really just, like, they stick, and they're not responsive enough.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.220
Yeah, you know when...

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:26.120
This is my first impression.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:31.740
You know when you have that dream where you have to, like, fight somebody, and then you suck at fighting?

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.720
Yeah, your arms are spaghetti.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:34.960
Right, your arms are spaghetti.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:37.340
That's how you feel playing this game.

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:43.880
As Daniel, for some reason, like, you can't, like, really move that well and kick at the same time.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:51.100
Or there's a lot of times where you go to, like, kick or punch, and you're just, like, what looks like a millimeter away from hitting the guy.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:55.200
I was wondering if you guys were going to talk about that because I thought maybe I was just being too picky.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.220
I was like, but I feel like I should be hitting him.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.660
They must be blocking.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:03.800
Like, there's definitely a sound effect that happens, but I don't know how to block.

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:08.960
I don't remember that being mentioned in the manual, but it wouldn't surprise me, I guess,

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:18.780
because to think that I'm always, like, throughout the entirety of the game, just a little bit off on each of my punches or kicks was very interesting to me.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:22.840
But I did like that the game starts by having you, you know, in the tournament.

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.100
Yeah. From...

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.160
The first one.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:26.300
The first move, yes.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:33.840
So you do get to start off with, like, a little recap of Karate Kid Part 1, even though you don't get to know that you're fighting, who's that kid, Johnny, right?

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:36.100
Johnny Lawrence. Johnny Lawrence from Cobra Kai.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.100
Yeah. You don't know that you're fighting him, right?

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:43.340
Like, in the finals. I mean, I knew that we were because I had just watched the movie, but it doesn't look like him.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:47.100
They could have just even said, though, like, finals versus Cobra Kai or something.

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:49.460
Yeah. I mean, at least he's wearing a black gi.

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:51.920
Yeah. I think that's the only thing that tips you off.

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:54.540
Okay. Yeah, I guess that's a better tell than nothing, though.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:57.060
I mean, it'd be weird if he showed up with a blue gi or something.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:04.580
So I guess we can go right into the gameplay then, because the tournament start, did you guys have a hard time getting through that?

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:06.540
It's like four or five rounds, right?

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:08.180
Yeah. I think it's four, right?

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.600
Four sounds right. It's four.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:17.540
I would usually get through the first three fights without dying, but the health you lose rolls over to the next fight.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:24.720
Which is weird to think about, that you don't get a chance to recover, but the ref's like, okay, next kid, get him now while he's down.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:26.060
And then they all have their full health.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.920
Like, weren't they fighting someone else before me?

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:34.300
I think it's recreating the idea that you are maimed several times in the movie.

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:37.220
Like, he gets his knee messed up.

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:39.460
Yeah, they go for his legs a lot in that movie.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.420
Yeah, sweep the legs. You're giving them a lot of credit.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:42.760
Yeah, I think that's why.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.060
I don't know, man.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.180
Sean's version is now canon.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:48.280
It has been accepted.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:57.840
I like it. But yeah, then I would usually die, or whatever, be defeated on the final round once.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:00.840
But you get three lives, so then I would obviously beat it the second time.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:02.220
And they're not lives, they're chances.

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:03.760
Chances, I'm sorry. Yeah, yeah.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:04.940
You get another chance.

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:07.420
I like the idea that the ref says, like, give him another gun.

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:09.360
Like, you sure you didn't beat him?

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:10.340
Like, get back in there.

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:17.060
But then also, this is an interesting segment because this is like Street Fighter-esque, right?

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:18.800
We haven't really seen too many things like this.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:24.000
You get the one-on-one where it's just, I thought that the whole game was going to be a fighting game.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.080
Well, that's what I thought, too.

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:29.680
And I thought it was going to be, oh, here's your first tournament, and then you go to World or something.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:31.520
Like every other, like, wrestling.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.840
Yeah, like a training level, and then back to the match.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:38.920
Makes sense. You could even get a little more creative with the enemies and do, like, you know, similar to Street Fighter,

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:42.560
where now all of a sudden it's like, there are guys who are regular humans, and then there's Blanka.

